user is asking about reading a tutorial related to GitHub, which seems to imply they want to develop skills associated with GitHub, possibly with the command line interface. I think it might be beneficial to use web_fetch for information instead of relying solely on memory. I’ll start by checking the skill file for the relevant GitHub details to ensure I'm providing the most accurate and useful guidance.\"}]}"},{"type":"text","text":"我先看这个仓库的 README 和相关配置，重点只抓：**他怎么配多个 agent、有哪些做法比我们更好。**","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_02a49797e73cc2790169bbc59eadd081918a598f48e1149718\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_thxL6GmB1e9VUcjI6kPdm1HV|fc_02a49797e73cc2790169bbc59eb9cc8191906b2ae7bb83f9dc","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/github/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"path\":\"~/.openclaw/workspace/skills/github/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":1396,"output":123,"cacheRead":97280,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":98799,"cost":{"input":0.0034900000000000005,"output":0.001845,"cacheRead":0.024319999999999998,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.029654999999999997}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1773913497863}}
{"type":"message","id":"723fa425","parentId":"ada0bc19","timestamp":"2026-03-19T09:45:03.014Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_thxL6GmB1e9VUcjI6kPdm1HV|fc_02a49797e73cc2790169bbc59eb9cc8191906b2ae7bb83f9dc","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: github\ndescription: \"Interact with GitHub using the `gh` CLI. Use `gh issue`, `gh pr`, `gh run`, and `gh api` for issues, PRs, CI runs, and advanced queries.\"\n---\n\n# GitHub Skill\n\nUse the `gh` CLI to interact with GitHub. Always specify `--repo owner/repo` when not in a git directory, or use URLs directly.\n\n## Pull Requests\n\nCheck CI status on a PR:\n```bash\ngh pr checks 55 --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nList recent workflow runs:\n```bash\ngh run list --repo owner/repo --limit 10\n```\n\nView a run and see which steps failed:\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo\n```\n\nView logs for failed steps only:\n```bash\ngh run view <run-id> --repo owner/repo --log-failed\n```\n\n## API for Advanced Queries\n\nThe `gh api` command is useful for accessing data not available through other subcommands.\n\nGet PR with specific fields:\n```bash\ngh api repos/owner/repo/pulls/55 --jq '.title, .state, .user.login'\n```\n\n## JSON Output\n\nMost commands support `--json` for structured output.  You can use `--jq` to filter:\n\n```bash\ngh issue list --repo owner/repo --json number,title --jq '.[] | \"\\(.number): \\(.title)\"'\n```\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773913502999}}
